WEBVTT

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.030
Miu, what are you...

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.870
I have feelings for Miu.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.170
I've always had feelings for her.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:25.630
Miu had feelings for you, but now she cares about me more.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.210
So we're dating now.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.130
I can't believe you'd do that to me!

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.000
You knew about Miu and me!

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.470
I knew things were rocky between you two.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:42.990
And I know just how much Miu was struggling with it.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.440
So I'm probably more—

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.580
Things were going fine with Miu!

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:47.440
We just went out—

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.190
Well, did you notice then?!

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:50.650
That she got a new haircut?!

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.550
Do you know when Miu's birthday is?

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.620
What about her favorite food or color?

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:06.250
It might be small, but if that's what makes her happy, then I'd—

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.250
That's enough.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.760
I don't want to hear it.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:13.040
But there's just one thing.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.460
Have you two kissed?

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:26.480
Miu!

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.300
<i>I'm not sad.</i>

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.580
<i>I'm frustrated.</i>

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.990
<i>Unbearably frustrated.</i>

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:12.960
Your body is out of line.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.870
Have you been skipping your weightlifting?

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:16.960
No, I've been doing it!

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:22.580
How many days has Tomo missed now?

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:23.720
Two weeks already.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.720
I text him every day, but...

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.100
Forget him.

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:32.230
If he wants to drop out, let him.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:35.780
We just have to focus on ourselves.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.780
When are you going to get over that?

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:44.780
Shut up.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.090
Who are you diving for?

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:12.480
Sorry.

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:17.470
If I heard you right, your girlfriend...

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:17.940
Yeah.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.940
...was stolen...

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:19.690
Yes.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:20.940
...by your younger brother?

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:25.460
And so you skipped two weeks of practice because you were depressed?

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:26.990
Yeah.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:30.410
You might not think it's a big deal, but to me—

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.300
Are you stupid?!

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:34.760
I'm not stupid.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:39.100
Hiroya might've been right that I
didn't pay enough attention to Miu,

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:42.420
but now that she's gone, I think I may've really liked her—

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.420
That's a lie.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:49.570
You just think you cared about her because you lost her.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:53.310
If she really was important,
you would've done that from the start.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.390
You would've made sure you wouldn't lose her.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:58.150
That's harsh.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:01.730
You're just running away from your problems by deceiving yourself.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:07.050
You already know what the most
important thing to you right now is.

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:13.700
Coach, you can say that because you focused your whole life on diving, and you've never fallen in love before!

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:22.210
I'm sorry.

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:27.930
You're right.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:31.430
I dedicated my life to diving.

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:36.640
I spent all of my time practicing,
but I wasn't able to become a top-tier diver.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:43.190
However, I had a natural intuition for diving.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:51.700
Warm-up

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:51.700
Jogging

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:51.700
Stretches

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:51.700
Weightlifting

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:51.700
Body alignment

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:51.700
Cool-down

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:47.370
Whether I'm performing myself, or watching others perform,

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:52.660
I can just tell what the flaws are, and how they can be fixed.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:56.710
And so I went to America and started studying how to coach.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:01.340
That's when my grandfather called me over to tell me

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:04.960
that he decided to create a diving club in Setagaya,

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:07.500
and he asked me if I'd coach.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:14.670
My grandfather said that after meeting a certain young man,
it rekindled his passion for diving.

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:15.980
Who do you think that was?

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:18.730
Okitsu Shibuki.

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:25.990
That's right, but he didn't join MDC.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:33.990
Then my grandfather passed away,
and I went to fulfill his unrealized dream.

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:35.780
And I thought I did.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:41.250
Then I also found another incredible talent named Fujitani Youichi here at MDC.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.500
I was sure.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.750
Okitsu Shibuki and Fujitani Youichi.

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:52.300
The two of them would be able to fire up MDC,
which had been saddling Mizuki.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:57.020
In other words, it was all for the two of them?

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:03.300
Fujitani wasn't the only talent I found in MDC.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:08.280
Unlike him, this boy was completely unpolished,

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:11.300
but he had the raw, natural talent.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:17.040
I'm talking about you, Sakai Tomoki.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:18.790
Me?

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:22.510
Yes. You have the natural talent.

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:24.370
I call them "diamond eyes."

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:26.110
Diamond eyes?

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:28.300
Do you remember?

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:30.680
Why did you stop at one?

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.180
I thought I was too slow.

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:36.350
When I see the five-meter platform there,

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:39.350
I won't make it unless I've already finished my second flip.

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:42.510
Your eyes are special.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:46.360
You're able to lock on to a target
while moving at incredible speeds.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:52.400
You had those special eyes, as well as flexibility, strength, and expressiveness.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.620
There aren't many athletes who have all these qualities.

00:07:56.090 --> 00:07:58.220
But you do.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:06.380
And that raw diamond is trying to throw away diving just because his brother stole his girl.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:11.570
He's closed himself inside this tiny room and is wasting his time wallowing every day.

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:14.890
So, what are you going to do?

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:17.410
Are you going to stay closed off?

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:18.640
Or will you...

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:22.630
Okay.

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:23.760
I see.

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:25.400
I was wrong.

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:31.330
You're not able to surpass the limits of this tiny world.

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:43.460
I'm coming in.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:46.140
I see you finally learned how to knock.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:49.680
Hey, I'm not an animal.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:51.210
Yeah, right.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:53.470
Tomorrow's the day.

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:54.220
Yeah.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:55.930
Want a massage?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:57.820
You trying to make me sick?

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.340
Hey, relax.

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:00.510
You've got a meet.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.160
I'm fine.

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:04.120
What were you thinking about?

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:04.980
Nothing.

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:06.680
Liar.

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:08.540
I can tell from your face.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:15.870
I just don't get it.

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:16.990
What do you mean?

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:21.740
I don't know why the old man taught me the diving standards.

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:24.520
Sakai Tomoki told me.

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:29.250
He said I knew all the basics needed for a meet before I even got here.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:33.800
Did the old man want to put me in a meet one day?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:37.010
Did he want me to repeat his failure?

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:41.380
Competitive Swimming Monthly

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:41.810
What grandpa would intentionally make his grandkid suffer?

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:49.270
Your grandpa didn't teach you the standard techniques to have you repeat his same mistakes.

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:55.790
Don't you think he only taught you the basics so you wouldn't repeat his failure?

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:57.030
What do you mean?

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:59.530
Just ask your own body.

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:05.450
There's only one thing I wish for.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.540
I want you to win tomorrow.

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:11.790
Not as a coach, but as your annoying roommate.

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:33.570
What are you doing?

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:35.410
I was remembering.

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:36.510
Remembering what?

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:39.970
The first time I ever saw one of these diving platforms.

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:43.400
Back then I was still eight.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:47.160
This platform looked like a giant dragon to me.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:53.090
Since then, I've sacrificed a lot in order to defeat this dragon.

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:57.590
My studies, school clubs, hanging out with my friends.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:00.820
You say that, but you still had a girlfriend.

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:02.240
Not anymore.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:08.100
Hiroya is the other life I could've had.

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:13.150
Hanging out with friends, really falling in love with someone.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:17.360
That must've been why I was so frustrated to have my girlfriend stolen from me.

00:11:18.230 --> 00:11:19.070
But...

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:20.250
But?

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:22.900
But I'm giving them up now.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:24.710
All the things I didn't choose.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:28.390
You'll do the three-and-a-half?

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:30.870
No, I'm going to surpass it.

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:34.630
Surpass the limits of this tiny world surrounding me.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:41.860
Diving first is Fujitani Youichi from Mizuki Diving Club.

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:44.090
Second is Atsuhiko Yamada.

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:46.360
They're about to start.

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:49.790
This competition is going to determine who gets to go to the Beijing camp.

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:50.980
We know.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:53.980
They're gonna pick the Olympic candidates at the camp, right?

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:57.230
What's wrong?

00:11:57.790 --> 00:11:59.410
You've got dead eyes.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:01.770
It's not my lucky day today.

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:04.990
Apparently Jupiter and Saturn
are ruining things for Sagittarius.

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:06.530
That's not it.

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:11.250
You may not want to accept it, but you're anxious.

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:13.570
You're scared.

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:14.000
What?

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:16.260
You can't help how scared you are.

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:19.000
Scared of proving yourself.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:35.750
Hey.

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:38.520
I'm not losing today.

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:42.780
I'll be waiting for you at the top, Fujitani Youichi.

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:45.780
Fujitani Youichi.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.780
Inward 3.5 Somersault Tuck

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:49.580
Representing the Mizuki Diving Club, 407C.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:51.290
Degree of difficulty: 3.2.

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:53.040
You can do it, Youichi!

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:05.550
Fujitani Youichi

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:05.550
That's Youichi for you. He already has a great score.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.800
Now, who's next?

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:12.060
It's so bright.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:15.890
Pinky!

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:22.860
Yamada Atsuhiko

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:22.860
Ibaraki Spirits

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:22.860
Back 2.5 Somersault 1.5 Twist Pike

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.860
Pinky might do it today.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.870
Maruyama Reiji

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.870
Reverse 2.5 Somersault Tuck

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:34.870
Oh, that's too bad.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:41.340
Oohiro Ryou

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:41.340
Forward 3.5 Somersault Pike

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:41.340
Oh man.

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:44.590
They both worked so hard too.

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:46.840
It's up to you now, Tomo.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:03.480
That was great, Tomo! Keep it up!

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:10.240
Come.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:13.790
Make it to the top.

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:17.250
Who was that again?

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:20.250
Matsuno from Tokushima?

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.750
Matsuno Kiyotaka

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.750
Mare Tokushima

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.750
Reverse 2.5 Somersault Pike

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:22.170
That was a good score, but...

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:23.750
Pretty plain.

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:26.670
Whoa, Tsuji's handstand is beautiful!

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.300
Here comes Fire Jirou!

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:38.850
He's still on fire today.

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:41.080
Okitsu is last.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:43.610
I hope he doesn't get too nervous, since this is his first meet.

00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:47.860
Damn it. Me, nervous?

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:49.920
You've gotta be joking!

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:51.620
The old man would laugh at me.

00:14:56.110 --> 00:14:59.870
Yo, old man. Tell me the truth.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:06.630
Your grandpa didn't teach you the standard techniques to have you repeat his same mistakes.

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:17.140
That was awesome! His entry was perfect!

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:22.800
In first place, Fujitani Youichi, 76.8.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:26.160
In second place, Okitsu Shibuki, 75.00.

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:28.150
Okitsu's in second?!

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:30.150
But something's not right.

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:32.550
Hey!

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:35.470
What's with the boring dive?!

00:15:35.470 --> 00:15:36.910
It's fine.

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:39.020
What's fine about it?!

00:15:39.020 --> 00:15:43.920
Did you come all the way from Tsugaru for that snoozefest?!

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.250
What?

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:47.170
Snoozefest?

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:48.980
What's wrong with it?

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:50.880
He's in second place after his first dive.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:51.910
It's a great start.

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:54.930
But anybody else could've done that dive!

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:58.700
You're the one who told me not to make any splashes.

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:02.080
Yeah, well, who told you to kill your personality to do it?!

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:04.440
Kill my personality?

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:10.440
I never said anything about pulling back on your
performance and killing what makes you unique!

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:15.450
Those big dives are out of the question right now.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:17.950
His back won't be able to—

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:20.700
How did you know?

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:25.710
Okitsu, what do you want to do?

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:31.970
If you keep doing easy dives,
you might get some decent results.

00:16:32.960 --> 00:16:33.640
But...

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:38.470
if you do your own brand of diving, even just once, in this competition,

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:41.930
if you learn the thrill of pushing yourself in front of a crowd,

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:45.350
you'll never forget that feeling for the rest of your life.

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:51.610
You'll be able to continue with diving, not for your promise to me, but for that momentary thrill.

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:55.270
Momentary thrill?

00:16:57.610 --> 00:17:00.360
Sakai Tomoki, 107B.

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:02.240
Degree of difficulty: 3.0.

00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:08.630
<i>I can make it!</i>

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:11.120
Yes!

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:22.640
Sakai Tomoki

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:22.640
Forward 3.5 Somersault Pike

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:24.510
That's a huge score!

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:25.640
That was amazing, Tomo!

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:29.900
Nice dive.

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:36.080
<i>In other words, you're scared.</i>

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:38.280
<i>You're scared of parting with the ocean.</i>

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:41.830
<i>You're scared of stepping into a new world.</i>

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:47.170
You have to do it.

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:51.090
You need to do it for yourself.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.070
Okitsu Shibuki

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.070
Back 3.5 Somersault Tuck

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:28.830
In first place, Fujitani Youichi, 342.00.

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.400
Did you see that?

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:32.280
That's Okitsu!

00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:35.090
What? But he fell to fourth place.

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:52.710
Look at that rip entry!

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:54.350
What was that again?

00:18:54.350 --> 00:19:00.240
Did you see how there was no splash, but there was that nice, loud plop?

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:03.160
Fujitani Youichi

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:03.160
Back 2.5 Somersault 1.5 Twist Pike

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:03.160
Three perfect scores!

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:04.910
This is getting interesting!

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.910
He's going way too far.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.420
Damn it.

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:26.930
Maruyama Reiji

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:27.970
Oohiro Ryou

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:31.430
Back 3.5 Somersault Tuck

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:08.220
All right!

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:18.550
That old man knew what this thrill felt like.

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:22.270
Okitsu Shibuki

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:22.270
Reverse 2.5 Somersault Pike

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:23.050
Now to announce the final standings.

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:27.240
In first place, Fujitani Youichi, 434.80.

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:29.750
In second place, Matsuno Kiyotaka...

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:42.270
Let's go, Tomo.

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:45.150
Hey, Tomo.

00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:46.850
I'm frustrated.

00:20:48.170 --> 00:20:55.440
Everyone complimented me on my fourth-place finish, but I didn't know how bad it felt to lose a competition.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:58.920
Ryou was right.

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:00.690
It can't just be fun.

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:03.700
I need to be first place.

00:21:04.250 --> 00:21:05.530
I want to win!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.830
I want to win next time and get first place!
